course: dictionary
lesson: 14941
title: Reheat and heat again
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To reheat means to heat food or drink again after it has gone cold. The clue is in the word: re- means again, and heat means make hot.
explain: «Mum will reheat the soup for lunch.» The soup was cooked, went cold, and now it gets hot again. Look for the clues: cold, then again, then hot.
explain: «Reheat the leftovers until they are piping hot all the way through.» Piping hot means steaming hot right through, not just warm on the outside. Good cooks check this, because it keeps food safe to eat.
explain: The prefix re- often means again. Once you know this, you can work out words like rewrite, redo and reread.
fact: Reheat is a verb: I reheat, she reheats, we reheated, they are reheating.
fact: Reheat means to heat food or drink again after it has gone cold.
fact: Reheat leftovers until they are steaming hot all the way through, to kill germs.
fact: Only reheat rice or chicken once, so cook only what you need.
fact: Microwaves reheat food quickly.
exercise: «Dad will reheat the pasta in the microwave.» What does reheat mean? | Throw away | *Heat again after it has gone cold | Cook for the first time | Put in the fridge to keep cold
exercise: «It takes 3 minutes to reheat one plate.» If you reheat 4 plates one at a time, how long will it take? | 10 minutes | *12 minutes | 7 minutes | 3 minutes
exercise: Which is the safest way to handle leftovers? | Eat them cold after a week | Reheat them until only warm on the outside | Leave them out all day | *Reheat them until steaming hot all the way through
test: Why should leftovers be steaming hot all the way through when you reheat them? | To make them look nicer on the plate | To make them go cold again | *To kill germs | To stop them smelling
test: The word reheat starts with re-. What does re- mean here? | Under | Before | *Again | Not
exam: Which sentence uses reheat correctly? | The reheat soup it has gone cold. | *Please reheat the soup, it has gone cold. | Please reheats the soup, it has gone cold. | Please reheated the soup, it has gone cold.
